  "infoPages": [
    {
      "id": "wsol26-arrival",
      "title": "Arrival & Check-in",
      "content": "Check-in opens Tuesday, December 15 at 2 PM in the Main Tent and stays open until 8 PM.\n\nBring your ticket QR code and a photo ID. You will receive a wristband that must stay on for the whole event.\n\n∙ Parking is next to the Main Lodge, follow the volunteers\n∙ Late arrivals: call the site number on your ticket\n∙ Quiet hours start at 9:30 PM across the whole site"
    },
    {
      "id": "wsol26-what-to-bring",
      "title": "What to Bring",
      "content": "Florida nights in December get down to the 40s°F (5°C), and Sadhana starts at 4 AM.\n\n∙ Yoga mat, meditation cushion and a sheepskin if you have one\n∙ Warm layers and a shawl for the early mornings\n∙ Flashlight or headlamp for the walk to the Main Tent\n∙ Reusable water bottle and a mug for Yogi Tea\n∙ White clothing for the Solstice night, if you wish"
    },
    {
      "id": "wsol26-white-tantric-yoga",
      "title": "White Tantric Yoga®",
      "content": "White Tantric Yoga® runs Thursday and Friday from 9 AM to 4:30 PM in the Tantric Shelter.\n\nPre-registration is required and separate from the event ticket.\n\n∙ Registration opens at 8:30 AM on Thursday\n∙ Doors close when a kriya begins and stay closed until it ends\n∙ Bring your own mat, a shawl and water\n∙ Wear white if you can, and no wristwatches during the kriyas"
    },
    {
      "id": "wsol26-gurdwara",
      "title": "Gurdwara",
      "content": "The Gurdwara is open all day for quiet meditation, with Kirtan each evening at 7:30 PM.\n\n∙ Cover your head and remove your shoes before entering\n∙ Everyone is welcome regardless of background\n∙ Please enter and leave quietly during Kirtan\n\nGurdwara Sahib with Langar is on Sunday at 11:15 AM."
    },
    {
      "id": "wsol26-site-and-safety",
      "title": "Site & Safety",
      "content": "Retreats By The Lake sits on Tiger Lake in Lake Wales, Florida.\n\n∙ First aid is at the Main Lodge, staffed 24 hours\n∙ Do not swim in the lake — it is not supervised and there is wildlife\n∙ Golf carts have right of way on the paths\n∙ Alcohol, smoking and drugs are not permitted anywhere on site\n∙ Emergency: dial 911, then notify the Main Lodge"
    },
    {
      "id": "wsol26-meals",
      "title": "Meals & Dietary Needs",
      "content": "All meals are vegetarian and served in the Dining Hall. Yogi Tea is available through the day.\n\n∙ Breakfast 6:30–8:00 AM · Lunch 12:00–1:30 PM · Dinner 5:30–7:00 PM\n∙ Gluten-free and vegan options at every meal\n∙ Severe allergies: speak to the kitchen lead on arrival\n∙ Please bring your own mug and water bottle"
    }
  ],
